>> title: Corn Bread Dressing
>> category: Vegetables & Sides
>> tags: cornbread, southern, baked, sage, side
>> counters: Meat and Three
>> aka: dressing, cornbread dressing, cornbread stuffing, corn bread stuffing, sage dressing
>> servings: 10
>> time: 1 hr 30 min
>> pairs-with: skillet-cornbread, turkey-pan-gravy, baked-turkey-wings, candied-yams
>> step.1: Bake this on a Tuesday. It is an everyday side at this counter rather than a once-a-year thing, which is why it is printed on the vegetable list beside the macaroni.
>> step.2: crumble, dry it out
>> step.3: sweat 10 min
>> step.4: stir to a loose batter
>> step.5: bake 375°F 50 min

Bake this on a Tuesday. It is an everyday side at this counter rather than a once-a-year thing, which is why it is printed on the vegetable list beside the macaroni.

Crumble @day-old skillet cornbread{8%cup}(900 g), @white sandwich bread{4%slices}(torn) onto a #sheet pan{} and leave them out to dry.

Sweat @unsalted butter{6%Tbs}(85 g), @yellow onion{1%large}(diced), @celery{4%ribs}(diced), @rubbed sage{1%Tbs}, @dried thyme{1%tsp}, @black pepper{1%tsp} in a #skillet{} for ~sweat{10%min}.

Stir @&(~2)dried crumbs{}, @&(~1)sweated vegetables{} with @chicken stock{4%cup}(950 mL), @large eggs{3}(beaten), @kosher salt{2%tsp} to a batter that pours slowly.

Bake @&(~1)dressing{} in a #9x13-in baking dish{} at 375°F (190°C) for ~bake{50%min}.

Pour a ladle of turkey pan gravy over the square once it is on the plate. Dressing on this board is served wet, and the difference between dressing and stuffing is that nothing here was ever inside a bird.
